  "summary": "The study uses few-layer Ti3C2Tx made by LiF/HCl etching and delamination, then compares pristine MXene, PMMA-template-sacrificed MXene, KOH-treated MXene, and combinations of these treatments. Four self-supporting composite electrodes containing carbonized in-situ-grown PAQ, resin, PVP, or PTh were compared in 3 M H2SO4. P-MXene/CPAQ-A was the headline and best electrode, reaching 532.9 F g\u22121 at 5 mV s\u22121, with 97.1% retention after 40,000 cycles at 20 A g\u22121. No BET surface area, pore-size distribution, porosity, mass loading, individual film thicknesses, or volumetric/areal capacitances were reported for the individual electrodes."
}